---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const seo = {
  title: "How to Track All Your Investments in One Place (India 2026) | Arthavi",
  description: "Complete guide to consolidating mutual funds, stocks, gold, fixed deposits, and real estate into one private portfolio dashboard in India.",
};

const schema = JSON.stringify({
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Article",
  "headline": seo.title,
  "description": seo.description,
  "datePublished": "2026-11-09",
  "dateModified": "2026-11-09",
  "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "Arthavi Editorial Team" }
});
---
<Layout
  title={seo.title}
  description={seo.description}
  keywords="track all investments in one place india, one place investment tracker, all investments dashboard india"
  schema={schema}
  breadcrumb={{
    items: [
      { name: "Home", url: "https://arthavi.com/" },
      { name: "Blog", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/" },
      { name: "Track All Investments in One Place", url: "https://arthavi.com/blog/track-all-investments-in-one-place/" }
    ]
  }}
>

<main class="container" style="padding-top: calc(var(--header-height) + 2rem); padding-bottom: 5rem;">
  <article class="prose fade-in" style="max-width: 820px; margin: 0 auto;">
    <h1>How to Track All Your Investments in One Place (India 2026)</h1>
    <p class="text-muted" style="font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7;">
      If you are like most Indian investors, your wealth is fragmented: mutual funds across multiple AMCs, stocks on Zerodha or Groww, Fixed Deposits across two banks, physical gold in a locker, and perhaps an ancestral property. Here is how to bring them all together.
    </p>

    <h2>The Problem with Modern Wealth Fragmentation</h2>
    <p>
      Managing investments across 4–6 separate logins causes severe blind spots:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Distorted Asset Allocation:</strong> You might think you have 70% in equity, but when factoring in FDs, EPF, and Gold, equity is actually under 45%.</li>
      <li><strong>Hidden Stock Overlap:</strong> Your Flexi Cap fund and Large Cap fund might both be heavily invested in the same banking stocks you hold directly in Zerodha.</li>
      <li><strong>Maturity &amp; Tax Surprises:</strong> Fixed deposits auto-renewing at sub-optimal interest rates or unharvested LTCG exceeding annual tax exemption thresholds.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>The 5 Steps to Complete Investment Consolidation</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Step 1: Consolidate Mutual Funds via CAS</strong> — Download a single CAMS/KFintech Consolidated Account Statement. Uploading it to Arthavi pulls all folios with complete transaction history.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 2: Import Equity Tradebooks</strong> — Export tradebooks from Zerodha, Groww, Upstox, or Angel One as CSV and import them without sharing broker credentials.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 3: Log Physical &amp; Digital Gold</strong> — Enter gold grams or SGB tranches. Arthavi links live bullion benchmarks into your net worth.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 4: Add Fixed Deposits &amp; PPF</strong> — Log bank FDs with interest rates and maturities to visualize debt allocation.</li>
      <li><strong>Step 5: Account for Property &amp; Liabilities</strong> — Track real estate valuation and deduct active home loans for net equity.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why Arthavi is the Ideal Multi-Asset Home</h2>
    <p>
      Unlike broker apps that only care about trades you execute with them, Arthavi is an <strong>independent, read-only portfolio intelligence platform</strong>. With our new <strong>CAS Delta Import</strong>, <strong>Portfolio Data Health</strong> indicators, and <strong>Family Wealth Snapshot</strong>, you get institutional clarity with zero spam calls or password sharing.
    </p>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin: 3rem 0;">
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/register" class="btn btn-primary" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; margin-right: 1rem;">Start Free Tracking</a>
      <a href="https://app.arthavi.com/demo" class="btn btn-demo" style="padding: 1rem 2.5rem; font-size: 1.1rem;">Try Demo</a>
    </div>

  </article>
</main>

</Layout>
